Modifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Original work: mtg-commander — a multi-agent Commander/EDH deck builder driven
by the Scryfall API, with a four-agent build pipeline (Deck Builder, Rules
Judge, Optimization Reviewer, Price Evaluator) and paired adversarial
challengers.

Modifications made 2026-10-18 by Paul Baker:

  - Added audit mode: evaluating an existing deck against EDHTop16 and
    cedhstats tournament data and producing a ranked swap sheet
    (SKILL.md "Audit Mode"; references/audit-guide.md).
  - Added scripts/deck_sources.py, scripts/meta_sources.py, and
    scripts/audit_compare.py.
  - Added partner commander support ("Partner", "Partner with", "Choose a
    Background", "Friends forever"): 98-card mainboard, union color identity,
    and a --partner flag on `validate-deck` (references/commander-rules.md,
    references/rules-judge-guide.md, references/intake-questions.md).
  - Added an `audit` block to the .mtg-commander.yml schema.
  - Added evals/evals.json.
  - Replaced runtime-specific instructions (Task-tool / omp references) with
    runtime-neutral sub-agent language.
  - Updated the trigger description in SKILL.md frontmatter to cover audit
    requests.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party services
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This skill talks to the following external services at runtime. It bundles none
of their content and requires no credentials for any of them:

  - Scryfall (api.scryfall.com) — card data and pricing.
  - Archidekt (archidekt.com) — deck import and Card Kingdom pricing.
  - Moxfield (api2.moxfield.com) — deck import.
  - cedhstats (cedhstats.org) — tournament card statistics.
  - EDHTop16 (edhtop16.com) — tournament entries, sourced from Topdeck.gg.
  - Jina reader (r.jina.ai) — optional fallback proxy used only when Moxfield
    blocks a direct request.

